card.statement:
Suppose $T_1,\ldots,T_n$ and $E_0,E_1,\ldots,E_n$ are elements of some skew field $\F$ containing $\K$ such that

\begin{align}
[T_i,T_j]&=0, \quad \forall i,j\in\iv{1}{n}, \\
[E_k,E_l]&=0, \quad \forall k,l\in\iv{0}{n},\\
T_j E_k -q^{\delta_{j+k>n}}E_kT_j &=
(q-1)\sum_{i\in\Z\setminus I(n-(j+k))} (-1)^{i+\delta_{i<0}}
E_{k+i} T_{j+i},
\end{align}

$\forall j\in\iv{1}{n}, k\in\iv{0}{n},$ where by convention
$T_j=0$ for $j\notin \iv{1}{n}$ and $E_k=0$ for $k\notin
\iv{0}{n}$. Define

\begin{align}
\widetilde{T}_j &=
\begin{cases}
E_jT_1T_n-(-1)^jE_0T_{n-j}T_1-(-1)^{n-j}E_nT_{n+1-j}T_n,& j\in\iv{1}{n-1}, \\
0,&\text{otherwise,}
\end{cases}\\
\widetilde{E}_k &=
\begin{cases}
T_{k+1},& k\in\iv{0}{n-1},\\
0,&\text{otherwise.}
\end{cases}
\end{align}

Then

\begin{align}
[\widetilde{T}_i,\widetilde{T}_j] &=0,\quad\forall i,j\in\iv{1}{n-1},\\
[\widetilde{E}_k,\widetilde{E}_l] &=0,\quad\forall k,l\in\iv{0}{n-1},
\end{align}

and, where
$\circ$ denotes the opposite multiplication
$a\circ b=ba$,

\begin{equation}
\widetilde{T}_j \circ \widetilde{E}_k -q^{\delta_{j+k>n-1}}\widetilde{E}_k \circ \widetilde{T}_j = (q-1)\sum_{i\in\Z\setminus I(n-1-(j+k))}
(-1)^{i+\delta_{i<0}} \widetilde{E}_{k+i} \circ \widetilde{T}_{j+i}
\end{equation}

for all $j\in\iv{1}{n-1}$, $k\in\iv{0}{n-1}$. Moreover, we have the following
alternative expression for $\widetilde{T}_j$:

\begin{equation}
q\widetilde{T}_j=
T_nT_1E_j-(-1)^{j}T_1T_{n-j}E_0-(-1)^{n-j}T_nT_{n+1-j}E_n,
\quad\forall j\in\iv{1}{n-1}
\end{equation}

which is equal to the right hand side of <<ref:eq:tilde_T_def>>
calculated in the opposite algebra. Furthermore, the set
$\{E_0,E_n\}\cup\{\widetilde{T}_j\}_{j=1}^{n-1}\cup\{\widetilde{E}_k\}_{k=0}^{n-1}$
generates the same skew subfield of $\F$ as the original generators
$\{T_j\}_{j=1}^n\cup\{E_k\}_{k=0}^n$.
